{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-005", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "France triples planned renewable energy auction volume to 1.5 GW", "content": "<p>France will increase the capacity of its upcoming technology-neutral renewable energy auction from 500 MW to 1.5 GW, opening the tender to all renewable power technologies and introducing a common baseload reference price for calculating payments to generators.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/france-triples-planned-renewable-energy-auction-volume-to-1-5-gw/\">France triples planned renewable energy auction volume to 1.5 GW</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/france-triples-planned-renewable-energy-auction-volume-to-1-5-gw/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-006", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Gambia signs four solar PPAs totalling 232 MW", "content": "<p>The Gambia’s state-owned utility has inked four large-scale solar power purchase agreements (PPAs) since late October, with battery storage included in each project.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/gambia-signs-four-solar-ppas-totalling-232-mw/\">Gambia signs four solar PPAs totalling 232 MW</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/gambia-signs-four-solar-ppas-totalling-232-mw/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-007", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Norwegian IPP shifts South African solar project to corporate buyers", "content": "<p>Norwegian independent power producer (IPP) Scatec said it plans to withdraw a 288 MW solar project from South Africa’s public renewables procurement program and sell it into the country’s growing corporate power market instead.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/norwegian-ipp-shifts-south-african-solar-project-to-corporate-buyers/\">Norwegian IPP shifts South African solar project to corporate buyers</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv ma", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/norwegian-ipp-shifts-south-african-solar-project-to-corporate-buyers/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-008", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Rare periods of low PV generation can be managed with storage", "content": "<p>The German Institute for Economic Research (DIW Berlin) says that batteries could help manage shortfalls in solar and wind generation, while underground storage of green hydrogen could provide backup during prolonged periods of low renewable output.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/rare-periods-of-low-pv-generation-can-be-managed-with-storage/\">Rare periods of low PV generation can be managed with storage</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.co", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/rare-periods-of-low-pv-generation-can-be-managed-with-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-009", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Spain could reach 10 GW of batteries by 2030, but bankability remains the major challenge", "content": "<p>The hybridization of solar PV plants, the evolution of arbitrage and ancillary services revenues, the future capacity market, and the financing of energy storage projects were the focus of a roundtable organized by <b>pv magazine</b> at Genera 2026. Experts anticipate strong growth in the Spanish market, though they warn of administrative hurdles, the lack of a revenue track record, and the complexity of managing these new assets. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/spain-could-reach-10-gw-of-batteries-by-2030-but-bankability-remains-the-major-challenge/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-010", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India adds 11.2 GW of rooftop PV capacity in first nine months of 2026", "content": "<p>India’s residential segment accounted for more than 95% of rooftop solar additions in the third quarter of 2026, driven by the government’s PM Surya Ghar program. Cumulative installed rooftop PV capacity reached 32 GW by the end of September.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/india-adds-11-2-gw-of-rooftop-solar-capacity-in-first-nine-months-of-2026/\">India adds 11.2 GW of rooftop PV capacity in first nine months of 2026</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/india-adds-11-2-gw-of-rooftop-solar-capacity-in-first-nine-months-of-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-011", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Estonian solar park energized with 55 MW/250 MWh battery", "content": "<p>Project developers say the battery energy storage system, which is tied to a 77.5 MW solar farm operational from 2024, features the Baltics’ largest battery system by storage capacity to date.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/estonian-hybrid-park-energized-with-55-mw-250-mwh-battery/\">Estonian solar park energized with 55 MW/250 MWh battery</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/estonian-hybrid-park-energized-with-55-mw-250-mwh-battery/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-012", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Huawei launches Luterra S2 in Europe", "content": "<p>The Luterra S2 uses 5 and 7 kWh battery modules featuring LFP technology and calls rated at 318 Ah. The 7 kWh module weighs 57 kg and provides 6.9 kWh of usable energy, while the 5 kWh module weighs 46 kg and provides 4.9 kWh. The system occupies 0.15 m2 of floor space and 0.69 m2 of wall space.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/huawei-launches-luterra-s2-in-europe/\">Huawei launches Luterra S2 in Europe</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/huawei-launches-luterra-s2-in-europe/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-013", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Switzerland raises incentives for solar below 100 kW", "content": "<p>Switzerland has increased one-time payments for PV systems below 100 kW by CHF 40 ($47.99)/kW and raised the rate for installations below 150 kW that do not consume their own electricity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/switzerland-raises-incentives-for-solar-below-100-kw/\">Switzerland raises incentives for solar below 100 kW</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/switzerland-raises-incentives-for-solar-below-100-kw/", "type": "rss"}]}
